ack and go into tablet mode  which gives you a much more convenient  touchscreen experience if that's what  you're into my biggest gripe about the  XPS S hinge is that it gets really stiff  before the display reaches a viewable  angle which is really annoying  appear to a very well-made hinge on the  surface in terms of keyboards the  surface has more key travel but it lacks  feedback whereas the keys on XPS have a  really good balance between key travel  and the nice springy feel that kind of  pushes back at you which makes it more  satisfying to type on I also love how  the XPS s keyboard goes edge to edge  while the surface has quite a bit of  waste of space on the sides now for the  track pads both are quite good but the  surface actually has a little bit more  of a satisfying feel getting into  speaker quality the surface laptop three  blows the XPS speakers out of the water  [Music]  now for the ports the surface keeps the  old school with a USB type a port a USB  sea ports in a MagSafe style charging  connector that quickly disconnects if  anybody trips over the cable the XPS on  the other hand comes with a Thunderbolt  3 port on each side and a mini SD card  slot the beauty of Thunderbolt 3 is that  you have a lot of extra bandwidth for  connecting things like high-speed SSDs  top-of-the-line accessories multiple 4k  displays and even external graphics  cards now let's compare performance  specs and value at three different price  points for $9.99 the surface laptop 3 is  a surprisingly good value getting 8 gigs  of ram and i5 processor with g7 graphics  and just 128 gigs of ram but more on  that in just a bit the XPS only gets 4  gigs of ram and i3 processor with g1  graphics but it does get 256 gigabytes  of storage  comparing processor performance the  surface definitely wins here especially  getting a huge boost and multi-core  score and the difference in graphics  performance is massive as well not only  is the surface a much better performer  at this price point it also comes with  the same good quality display as the  top-end spec whereas the lower price  Dells come with a 1200 P display which  kind of seals the deal for the surface  now at the $1,300 price point the  surface gets full aluminum and 256  gigabytes of storage whereas the XPS  gets a gigs of ram and an i5 processor  but the same slow graphics so the  surface pro is still a better Buy if you  don't need Thunder both three now every  other option above $1,300 comes with the  same i7 processor and graphics so the  surface loses its performance advantage  and the lack of Thunderbolt 3 and the  more reflective display really starts to  stand out the higher-end dulles can come  with 4k displays which are sharper more  color accurate and less reflective at a  trade-off in battery life which the  surface laptop 3 comes in right in  between around 8 hours of real world use  you can even get 32 gigabytes of RAM on  the XPS which most people don't need but  if you plan to connect and  GPU for video editing or run other  programs that can utilize this Ram such  as Lightroom classic this extra Ram can  really help quite a bit  the surface does have a trick up its  sleeve which is the SSD that isn't a  standard design and although it's not  easy to access it can actually be  swapped out in the future  which is really nice especially if you  buy the base model at the lower price  points if you don't need Thunderbolt 3 I  would definitely buy the surface because  of its minimalistic but premium design  great performance instant Windows hello  facial recognition and the excellent  hinge and also the much louder speakers  but if you're looking at the high-end  configs we would suggest XPS because it  does offer a better display potentially  more RAM and Thunderbolt 3 no matter  which laptop you prefer we will have  links the best deals on both of them  down in the description below if you  enjoyed this comparison tap like and  click that circle above to subscribe for  more videos and you guys can see the  full reviews of both of these laptops  right over there there's been max max  tech and I will see you in the next  video  [Music]

